TPV102 v9.2.0 plan §5.1 — SEAS_DIAG_FAULT_SIGMA C0 diagnostic patch
====================================================================

This is a STANDALONE DIFF.  It is NOT YET APPLIED.  Per plan §5.1 and
the TODO checklist head of tpv102_debug_v9.2.0_debug_plan.md, user
approval is required before the debugger applies this patch.

Purpose (§5.1 rank-1 diagnostic)
--------------------------------
Adds ONLY printfs + MPI_Allreduce.  No functional code changes.
Measures `max|Q_self[SYY]|`, `max|Q_self[VY]|`, `max|Q_self[SYZ]|`,
`max|Q_self[VZ]|` on ALL fault QPs, reduced across ranks, printed to
stderr once per RK4 step.

Why this matters for R-V92 diagnosis
------------------------------------
The observed σ_n drift is 50 MPa.  The diagnostic discriminates
between:

- bulk mode-II σ_yy amplification (H-V92-G): max|Q_self[SYY]| on
  fault QPs tracks the drift magnitude.
- RK4 stage-averaging bug in station output (H-V92-K): bulk stays
  clean (~0 MPa), station sigma_n_corr still drifts.

Apply with:
    cd /Users/chunhuizhao/projects/seas-mfem
    patch -p0 < miniapps/seas/debug_document/tpv102_debug_document/tpv102_debug_v9.2.0_diag_fault_sigma.patch

Revert with:
    patch -R -p0 < miniapps/seas/debug_document/tpv102_debug_document/tpv102_debug_v9.2.0_diag_fault_sigma.patch

Build with the flag enabled:
    cd miniapps/seas
    make seas_tpv102_driver SEAS_EXTRA_CPPFLAGS="-DSEAS_DIAG_FAULT_SIGMA"

Expected stderr output shape (one line per RK4 Mult call):
    [FAULT-DIAG-SYY] t=0.000 max|SYY|=0.000e+00 max|VY|=0.000e+00 max|SYZ|=0.000e+00 max|VZ|=0.000e+00
    ...
    [FAULT-DIAG-SYY] t=3.500 max|SYY|=4.123e+07 max|VY|=2.345e-02 ...

Verification
------------
After applying, `make test` on the local laptop should STILL pass
(the patch is compile-only-additive; runtime behavior depends on
SEAS_DIAG_FAULT_SIGMA flag which is off by default in `make test`).

--- miniapps/seas/dynamic/wave_operator.inl.orig
